{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #376: declared status 'open'. Formalized: yes. Are there infinitely many $n$ such that $\\binom{2n}{n}$ is coprime to $105$? Current best: The best result in this direction is due to Bloom and Croot \\cite{BlCr25}, who proved that, if $p_1,p_2,p_3$ are sufficiently large primes, then there are infinitely many $n$ such that almost all of the base $p_i$ digits are $<p_i/2$. Prize: no. OEIS: A030979. Tags: base representations, binomial coefficients, number theory."},"claim_id":"vcl_0f82bbd7343d77327d1243a1750837b1f20c50402383aff88eb5bbcf78fc5beb","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:376","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_0f554e13c928d569","object_root":"sha256:5e4a27a6ff06614069abbff9cb095dec37e9ab515395b685f55200740d063036","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:376"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}